From d5bf132d4a38c91255a2e9e88732eadd9770742b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daliborlol <dalibor@pyro.tf>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 00:46:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix: clip overlays onto displacements and faces with
 collinear first corners

Overlays whose target faces are displacements were skipped. They are now
projected into the base face plane and clipped per displacement triangle,
each clipped vertex moved onto the displaced surface by its barycentric
coordinates (positions, normals and lightmap coordinates).

clip_polygon took the clip polygon's winding from its first three corners;
compiled faces often start with collinear corners (T-junction fixes), which
gave a zero or wrong sign and clipped every overlay away. The winding now
comes from the polygon's area.

pl_vigil_rc10: 135 -> 152 of 161 overlays handled (9 have malformed face
lists); koth_product_final: 62 -> 94 of 94.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
